# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values

BOTTOKEN={Discord Bot Token}
WEBHOOKCHANNEL={No longer used: keep it a valid webhook while an older image may be rolled back to}
TENORKEY={Optional Tenor API Key (optional)}
STEAMWEB_KEY={Steam Web API Key}
STEAMWEB_PUB_KEY={Steam Publisher Key (Only for MM devs with Steam developer access)}
STEAMUSER_NAME={Your Steam Username}
STEAMUSER_PASSWORD={Your Steam Password}
STEAM_QRCODE_AUTH=true
STEAMUSER_REMEMBERME=true
STEAMAPP_ID=274900
ALERT_USER_ID={Discord user ID that gets the bot's alerts (optional, the application's owner by default)}

# The key the bot checks each of the dashboard's requests against: 64 hexadecimal digits in small letters, the same as the
# dashboard's Dashboard__RequestSigningKey. On the server, setup-dashboard.sh makes it and writes both. Empty turns the
# dashboard's requests off, and the bot refuses each one, saying why.
REQUEST_SIGNING_KEY=

# The website's database (armor, blacklist and server channels), and MinerBot's own database, where the bot records its
# status and history, keeps a copy of its servers and keeps the record of its posts. Without BotConnection the bot runs
# and posts, keeping that record in memory, so a restart loses what it hasn't posted yet, and records nothing.
# CharSet=utf8mb4 is the tables' own character set, so emoji aren't sent as question marks.
# The dashboard writes audit and review rows on the website's connection, and a move back to pending from Approved reads
# MinerBot's record of the armor's posts there, so the dashboard's DefaultConnection login also needs INSERT on
# MinerBot's audit_log and armor_reviews tables and SELECT on its notification_seen, notification_queue,
# notification_deliveries and guild_delivery_status tables, unless both use one login with rights on both databases.
ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection=SERVER={Server Host};PORT=3306;DATABASE={Website Database Name};UID={User ID};PASSWORD={Password};SSLMODE=Preferred;Connection Timeout=30;CharSet=utf8mb4;
ConnectionStrings__BotConnection=SERVER={Server Host};PORT=3306;DATABASE={MinerBot Database Name};UID={User ID};PASSWORD={Password};SSLMODE=Preferred;Connection Timeout=30;CharSet=utf8mb4;
